//for basic html setup you are starting with <!DOCTYPE html>. This defines it as a HTML document.
//Next up is <html></html> which is quite the back burner, you just put all your html related stuff in there. 

//The <head></head> is where you put your title to name the document and links relating to ur css.
// As just mentioned, the <title></title> is where you put your browser name.
//<link rel href></link> is where you link to css/javascript. It can also be used to add an icon to your browser tab.

//The <body></body> is after you finish your head, and it will contain your nav and main.
//In <nav></nav> this gives you an area typically at the top of your screen, where you will link things for navigation. headers and stuff can be added here.
//<main></main> is where all of your juciy stuff occurs; your images, your heading, your list, your paragraph, your everything really.
//<div></div> is used to create seperations on pages, so that they are not grouped together. Think of it like pressing enter a few time to seperate paragraphs. To seperate these things into seperate blocks, you would divide the nav from the main.
//<h1></h1> is just a header. the bigger the number the smaller the font.
//<p></p> is just paragraphs.
//<a href></a> anchors a link to a object or text, so that when click it takes you somewhere. Like a hyperlink.... BLOCKED?!?!??!?
//<ul></ul> is used to establish a list is being formatted.
//<li></li> is used to make a list in a ul element.
//<img href></img> is used to make images.


